# PART 2 — CATALOG OF WORKS MANAGEMENT

## 2.1 Create a Dedicated Catalog Management Page

Create a dedicated navigation menu named:

**CATALOG OF WORKS MANAGEMENT**

This must be the central administration area for managing all construction work categories, individual materials, labor items, services, and reusable Sets of Works.

Users must not need to open a quotation to create or edit catalog records.

The Catalog Management page must have two main sections:

**A. Individual Items Catalog**

A master database of individual materials, construction supplies, labor components, equipment, and services.

**B. Sets of Works Catalog**

A master database of reusable construction work assemblies containing predefined materials, labor, equipment, and other applicable components.

Provide separate tabs for these two sections.

## 2.2 Individual Items Catalog

Create a searchable and manageable master list of individual construction items.

Each item must contain:

- Unique Item ID.
- Item Code / SKU.
- Item Name.
- Category.
- Item Description.
- Technical Specifications.
- Unit of Measurement.
- Item Type: Material, Labor, Equipment, Service, or Other.
- Supplier/Vendor associations.
- Supplier purchase prices.
- Default cost, where applicable.
- Default pricing configuration, where authorized.
- Active or Inactive status.
- Remarks.
- Supporting documents or photographs, where applicable.

Authorized users must be able to:

- Add New Item.
- Edit Existing Item.
- View Item Details.
- Duplicate Item.
- Archive or deactivate an item.
- Restore archived items.
- Search and filter records.
- Import and export catalog data, where supported.

Allow administrators to add and manage categories, units of measurement, and item classifications.

Prevent duplicate items by checking existing item codes, names, specifications, and relevant matching records.

## 2.3 Work Categories

Create configurable categories for construction works.

Initial categories should include:

- Masonry Works
- Tiling Works
- Painting Works
- Carpentry Works
- Plumbing Works
- Electrical Works
- Concrete Works
- Waterproofing Works
- Ceiling Works
- Roofing Works
- Metal Works
- Fabrication Works
- Custom Works

Administrators must be able to create additional categories, rename categories, rearrange their display order, and deactivate obsolete categories.

Categories must not be hard-coded.

## 2.4 Sets of Works — Reusable Construction Assemblies

Create a dedicated function called:

**SETS OF WORKS**

A Set of Works is a reusable construction work assembly containing all the materials, labor, equipment, and other components required for a particular construction activity.

Each assembly must be saved in the master catalog so it can be reused in future quotations.

Examples:

**Masonry Works**
- Interior Wall Construction
- Exterior CHB Wall
- Pantry Counter
- Concrete Partition
- CHB Wall with Plastering

**Tiling Works**
- Floor Tiling
- Wall Tiling
- Bathroom Floor Tiling
- Kitchen Backsplash

**Painting Works**
- Interior Wall Painting
- Exterior Wall Painting
- Ceiling Painting
- Metal Surface Painting

**Carpentry Works**
- Cabinet Installation
- Door Installation
- Custom Woodwork

**Plumbing Works**
- Waterline Installation
- Drainage Installation
- Plumbing Fixtures

**Electrical Works**
- Lighting Installation
- Power Outlet Installation
- Electrical Wiring

Allow unlimited additional assemblies within each category.

## 2.5 Work Assembly Template Information

Each Set of Works must contain:

- Unique Assembly Code.
- Assembly Name.
- Work Category.
- Description.
- Technical Specifications.
- Unit of Measurement.
- Default Calculation Method.
- Default Quantity or Consumption Rate.
- List of included materials.
- List of included labor components.
- Optional equipment and other cost components.
- Preferred suppliers for applicable materials.
- Default wastage percentages, where applicable.
- Labor requirements.
- Installation instructions.
- Notes.
- Template Version.
- Active or Inactive status.

All assembly components must be editable.

Do not hard-code materials, labor quantities, or calculation formulas for specific work categories.

## 2.6 Visual Assembly Editor

Create an easy-to-use visual editor for creating and modifying Sets of Works.

The editor must allow users to:

- Search for existing items in the Individual Items Catalog.
- Add multiple materials.
- Add labor components.
- Add equipment or services.
- Remove components.
- Rearrange component order.
- Change quantities.
- Change units of measurement.
- Specify material requirements.
- Select preferred suppliers.
- Set consumption rates.
- Add wastage percentages.
- Add technical notes.
- Preview the complete assembly.
- Save the assembly as a reusable template.

Provide an **ADD ITEM** function that allows users to insert as many components as necessary.

If an item does not exist in the Individual Items Catalog, authorized users must be able to create a new item without losing the assembly currently being edited.

## 2.7 Example: Interior Wall Construction

Create the capability to configure an assembly such as:

**Category:** Masonry Works

**Set of Works:** Interior Wall Construction

**Description:** Construction of an interior CHB partition wall, including reinforcement, mortar, and associated materials.

Possible components:

| Material / Component | Type | Unit | Default Quantity |
|---|---|---|---|
| CHB 4 inches | Material | pcs | Configurable |
| Reinforcing bars | Material | lengths | Configurable |
| GI tie wire | Material | kg | Configurable |
| Cement | Material | bags | Configurable |
| Sand | Material | cu.m. | Configurable |
| Mason | Labor | day | Configurable |
| Helper | Labor | day | Configurable |

These are examples only. The administrator must determine the actual materials, quantities, specifications, and labor requirements.

## 2.8 Example: Pantry Counter Construction

Allow another independent assembly:

**Category:** Custom Works or Masonry Works

**Set of Works:** Pantry Counter Construction

Possible components:

- CHB or concrete support materials.
- Reinforcing bars.
- GI tie wire.
- Cement.
- Sand.
- Cement board or other specified substrate.
- Tile adhesive.
- Countertop finishing materials.
- Labor.
- Other project-specific components.

The user must be able to define a completely different set of materials for this work.

## 2.9 Measurement-Based Calculations

Allow Sets of Works to calculate required material quantities based on the measurement of the work.

Support:

- Fixed quantities.
- Quantity per square meter.
- Quantity per linear meter.
- Quantity per cubic meter.
- Quantity per piece.
- Other configurable calculation methods.

Example:

If the user selects Interior Wall Construction and enters 25 square meters, the system calculates material requirements using the consumption rates configured in the assembly.

The calculation must be visible and explainable.

Allow authorized estimators to override calculated quantities.

Do not assume that all construction work uses the same calculation formula.

## 2.10 Custom Work Assemblies

Allow authorized estimators to create a custom Set of Works directly inside the Quotation Editor.

Provide two save options:

1. Save for this quotation only.
2. Save as a reusable Set of Works in the master catalog.

If saved to the master catalog, the assembly must be available for future quotations.

Changes to quotation-specific assemblies must not automatically change master catalog records.

