# PART 3 — CATALOG VERSION CONTROL AND PERMISSIONS

## 3.1 Version Control

Implement version tracking for Sets of Works.

When a master assembly is edited:

- Save a new version.
- Record who made the change.
- Record the date and time.
- Preserve the previous version.
- Allow authorized users to view previous versions.
- Provide a comparison of changes between versions.
- Allow new quotations to use the latest active version by default.

Previously prepared or approved quotations must retain their original assembly contents, quantities, descriptions, supplier information, costs, and calculations.

Updating the master catalog must never silently modify historical quotations.

## 3.2 Catalog Permissions

Provide granular permissions:

- View Catalog.
- Create Individual Items.
- Edit Individual Items.
- Manage Categories.
- Create Sets of Works.
- Edit Sets of Works.
- Duplicate Sets of Works.
- Archive Catalog Records.
- Restore Archived Records.
- Manage Supplier Associations.
- Manage Supplier Prices.
- Override Material Costs.
- View Internal Cost Information.

An estimator may have permission to use catalog records in quotations without having permission to edit the master catalog.

If an estimator identifies a missing item, provide an option to request its addition by an authorized catalog administrator.

All permissions must be enforced by the backend.

