# PART 7 — PURCHASE REQUEST: MULTIPLE ITEMS IN ONE REQUEST

## 7.1 Multi-Item Purchase Request

Enhance the existing Purchase Request module to support both single-item and multiple-item requests.

A user must be able to create one purchase request containing several different materials or products.

Do not require separate purchase requests for every item.

## 7.2 Purchase Request Header

Each request must contain:

- Purchase Request Number.
- Request Date.
- Requesting Project.
- Project Site.
- Requesting Department.
- Requesting Employee.
- Required Delivery Date.
- Preferred Supplier, if applicable.
- Purpose or Justification.
- General Remarks.
- Attachments.
- Overall Status.

## 7.3 Multiple Line Items

Allow users to dynamically add as many line items as required.

Each line item must contain:

| Field | Description |
|---|---|
| Item Code | Existing catalog code, if available |
| Item Description | Material or product name |
| Specifications | Size, brand, model, or requirements |
| Quantity | Requested quantity |
| Unit | Unit of measurement |
| Estimated Unit Price | Expected cost |
| Estimated Total | Quantity × estimated unit price |
| Preferred Supplier | Supplier selection |
| Remarks | Item-specific notes |

Users must be able to:

- Add line items.
- Remove line items before submission.
- Edit quantities.
- Change units.
- Search the existing inventory catalog.
- Search suppliers.
- Add new items, subject to permissions.
- Add item-specific remarks.
- Attach specifications and supporting documents.

## 7.4 Automatic Calculations

Calculate automatically:

- Line item totals.
- Number of requested line items.
- Estimated total purchase request amount.

Recalculate whenever quantities or prices change.

Validate numerical values and prevent invalid negative quantities or prices.

## 7.5 Purchase Request Approval

The approval interface must display all requested items in one organized table.

Approvers must be able to:

- Approve all items.
- Reject all items.
- Partially approve selected items.
- Modify approved quantities, subject to authorization.
- Return the request for correction.
- Add remarks to individual items.
- Add general approval remarks.

Maintain requested quantities separately from approved quantities.

A partially approved request must clearly show the approval status and approved quantity for each line item.

## 7.6 Procurement and Delivery Tracking

After approval, connect the request to the existing procurement workflow.

Procurement personnel must be able to:

- Assign suppliers to individual items.
- Compare supplier quotations.
- Record actual purchase prices.
- Generate purchase orders or procurement records.
- Track ordered quantities.
- Track partial deliveries.
- Record actual quantities received.
- Attach supplier invoices and delivery receipts.
- Record delivery discrepancies.

The system must maintain traceability:

**Purchase Request → Approval → Purchase Order → Supplier → Delivery → Warehouse Receiving → Inventory Stock**

Do not automatically increase warehouse stock when a request is submitted or approved.

Only physically received and accepted deliveries may increase warehouse inventory.

