# PART 9 — SHARED FILE AND PHOTO MANAGEMENT

All modules must use a secure, consistent attachment management system.

Requirements:

1. Store uploaded files in protected storage.
2. Do not expose private financial receipts or internal project photographs through public file URLs.
3. Validate file types and sizes.
4. Generate unique filenames.
5. Prevent executable file uploads.
6. Support image compression and thumbnail generation.
7. Preserve original photographs where required for audit or financial evidence.
8. Associate every attachment with its corresponding record.
9. Enforce file permissions on the server.
10. Maintain attachment history.
11. Support authorized viewing and downloading.
12. Prevent unauthorized deletion of approved financial and task evidence.

The application must remain compatible with GoDaddy cPanel shared hosting.

Do not introduce mandatory external storage, expensive third-party services, or a separate continuously running Node.js server.

